\pard\f2\b\fs28\fi-1020\li1200\fc0\cf0 Protocol Description\

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\f0\b0\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 The NSDecimalBehaviors protocol declares three methods that control the discretionary aspects of working with NSDecimalNumbers. The 
\b scale
\b0  and 
\b roundingMode
\b0  methods determine the precision of NSDecimalNumber's return values, and the way in which those values should be rounded to fit that precision. The 
\b exceptionDuringOperation:error:leftOperand:rightOperand:
\b0  determines the way in which an NSDecimalNumber should handle different calculation errors.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 For an example of a class that adopts the NSDecimalBehaviors protocol, see the specification for NSDecimalNumberHandler.\

\fs14 \

